here's a needlepoint  hanging on her wall that says we must be  cut to heal and that and other details  like how she drives a white rabbit are  really working for me mark settles in to  watch some tv and catches a debate about  severed employees the company line is  that severance is a choice that  employees should be allowed to make and  we'll see this new character natalie who  is very good at arguing in favor of it  later in the episode the next morning we  get reminded about how messed up it  actually is mark says that he won't be  reintegrating because it helps him deal  with his wife's death and in response to  this petey reveals that mark used to  come into the office with red eyes so  often that they had a joke about him  having an elevator allergy he was crying  in his car in the first episode and that  almost makes it seem like it's part of  his pre-work routine he's climbing the  corporate ladder though and on his first  day of reading the announcements rather  than interrupting them with his gas  habbing he has to break it to hely that  her audi denied her resignation request  back at his place rickens stops by to  drop off his new book which is  intercepted by harmony then she sneaks  into the house petey does hear her come  in so he's able to hide initially but  when she gets a call he starts to freak  out and leaves before she goes she gets  into the box that's filled with his  wife's crafts and takes the candle we  saw him look at whenever he was in there  before also petey starts looking at the  map and that leads him to wander away  from the safety of mark's house back at  the office heli is still trying to get a  message to her audi and she comes up  with what seemed to be fairly ingenious  ideas breaking the writing up on both of  her arms and swallowing the note inside  a makeshift capsule what really stands  out here is that mark not only picks up  on what she's doing but instantly has a  negative consequence at the ready in his  effort to talk her out of it where we  are it's a little hard to wrap your head  around how the code detector might  actually do the things they say it does  but what does it mean that these methods  have already been attempted the mention  of bad soap and milk check having to  know what end to try to extract the  capsule from hint that most people try  to resist being severed in the same ways  it's possible he's just making things up  to scare her but i find these little  details to be some of the most  fascinating things that we learned in  this episode  irv believes what heli needs is a deeper  meaning and suggests they go to the  perpetuity wing on the way there they  run into optics and design for one of  the funniest scenes of the series so far  really this whole trip out of the office  was super entertaining the tribal nature  of the groups dylan's antagonism that  felicia gives right back the chemistry  between irv and burt it's all working  here i laughed out loud at pretty much  everything dylan said on this excursion  while they're out natalie from the tv  debate does come in to see harmony we  get another one of these awkward  encounters where the board silently  listens while they wait for the person  to go first she tries to bring up that  there may have been some signs of  reintegration before he left but they  quickly shut her down and then we also  get the idea that there is some concern  that the department might not make their  numbers the perpetuity wing is about as  spooky as you would imagine but is also  somewhat believable at the same time  you've got wax figures of all eight ceos  from the 150 year plus history and a  complete replica of the founder kier  egan's home as much as herb is  enthralled by the history of it all it  doesn't work for heli and she uses the  opportunity to make another escape  attempt this time when she runs into a  locked door she smashes out the window  with a fire extinguisher that sets off  alarms and what i think she's trying 